# Nail Feed (`/nail-feed`) — Route Reference

This document is for whoever writes the content-generation prompts that
produce Nail Feed posts. It describes every frontmatter field, what happens
if you omit one, how the page renders top to bottom, and the hard
technical constraints (Discover eligibility) the content must satisfy.

Nail Feed is **not** `/blog`. It is a separate, purpose-built route for
Google Discover traffic — fast, opinionated, short-form posts, distinct
from `/blog`'s SEO-depth pillar/cluster content. Do not reuse `/blog`
frontmatter conventions or word-count targets here; several are
deliberately different, noted below.

---

## 1. File location & slug

Posts are `.md` (or `.mdx`) files in:

```
src/content/nailfeed/{slug}.md
```

The **filename (without extension) is the slug**, and it is used directly
in the URL: `src/content/nailfeed/chrome-french-tips-are-back.md` →
`https://mirelleinspo.com/nail-feed/chrome-french-tips-are-back`.

Routing is **flat** — there is no topic-folder nesting like `/blog`'s
`/blog/[topic]/[slug]`. Do not create subfolders per topic; `topic` is a
frontmatter field only (see below), not a URL segment.

---

## 2. Frontmatter field reference

### Required

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `title` | string | Falls back to `"Untitled"` if omitted — **always set this.** |
| `date` | string (ISO date) | Falls back to the current date/time if omitted — **always set this**, posts are sorted newest-first by this field. |

Nothing else is strictly required by the code (everything else has a
fallback), but omitting the fields below produces a visibly broken or
Discover-ineligible page. Treat the table below as required in practice.

### Strongly expected (fallbacks exist but will look wrong/broken if skipped)

| Field | Type | Fallback if omitted | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `excerpt` | string | `''` (empty) | Used as meta description, OG/Twitter description, and listing-page card text. Write one — don't skip it. |
| `author` | string | `'Mirellé Team'` | **Must be exactly `"Jyotika Verma"` or `"Gaurav Verma"`** (or a string containing `"jyoti"`/`"jyotika"`, or `"gaurav"`). See §6 — this is name-matched, not slug-matched, and the match logic is loose substring matching. Do not invent new author names; only these two authors currently resolve to a real profile (headshot, bio, socials). Anything else silently renders **no author card at all.** |
| `image` | string (path) | `null` — hero renders broken | Hero image path, e.g. `/images/nailfeed/chrome-french-tips.jpg`. See §5 for the hard size/aspect requirement. |
| `imageAlt` | string | falls back to `title` | Always write real alt text — accessibility + image SEO. |
| `imageWidth` | number | `1200` | Should always be `1200` — see §5. |
| `imageHeight` | number | `675` | Should always be `675` — **not** 630 (that's `/blog`'s ratio). See §5. |
| `category` | string | `undefined` | Free text, used for the listing-page filter (`/nail-feed?category=...`) and shown as a small label above the H1. No fixed enum — but stay consistent with existing values in use (e.g. `"Trends"`). |
| `readTime` | string or number | `'4 min'` | Nail Feed posts are short — realistic values are usually `"2 min"`–`"5 min"`. |
| `canonical` | string (full URL) | auto-built as `https://mirelleinspo.com/nail-feed/{slug}` | Only set this manually if the canonical URL needs to differ from the default (rare — e.g. syndicated content). |

### Optional — content structure

| Field | Type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `tldr` | object | Powers the `WrapUp` card rendered directly under the hero, before the body. See §3 for its full shape (`summary`, `keyTakeaways`, `tldrFaqs`). Highly recommended — this is the "direct-answer intro" the whole Discover strategy depends on. |
| `faqItems` | array of `{question, answer}` | Powers a separate, fuller **FAQ section** further down the page (after the body, before the final newsletter). **Distinct from `tldr.tldrFaqs`** — do not duplicate the same Q&As in both; `tldrFaqs` should be short teasers, `faqItems` the fuller answers. See §3. |

### Optional — topic/relational (SEO structure, not required per-post)

| Field | Type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `topic` | string (slug-like) | Links this post conceptually to a `/blog` pillar topic (e.g. `"chrome-nails"`) and groups related Nail Feed posts on the listing page (`/nail-feed?topic=...`). Use the **same slug** as the corresponding `/blog` pillar topic where one exists. |
| `topicalMap.parentPillar` | string (path) | The `/blog` pillar URL this post should link back to editorially, e.g. `"/blog/chrome-nails"`. This is data only — nothing auto-injects the link into body content; if the post should link back, write that link into the Markdown body yourself. |
| `topicalMap.relatedClusters` | string[] | Slugs of **other Nail Feed posts** (not `/blog` posts) that are siblings on the same topic. Used by the "Read More" rail as the *first* priority match — see §4. |
| `topicalMap.primaryKeyword` | string | Free-text SEO note, not rendered anywhere currently — informational for planning only. |
| `topicalMap.secondaryKeywords` | string[] | Same — informational only. |
| `topicalMap.topicalBoundary` | string | Free-text note describing what this post does/doesn't cover, useful for keeping a topic cluster non-overlapping. Informational only, not rendered. |

Do **not** add: `position`, `hierarchyLevel`, `childClusters`,
`contentType`, `semanticRelationships`, `contentMetrics`,
`showInspoGalleryLink`, `template`, `tutorialMetadata`, `videoMetadata`,
`eventData`, `carouselImages`, `products`, `heroImages` (plural). These
are `/blog`-only concepts (pillar/cluster hub pages, multiple templates,
inspo gallery links, tutorial/video/event schema, product grids/carousels)
that Nail Feed deliberately does not support. Setting them does nothing —
no code reads them.

